`@superfunctions/http` is used in **one place** under `client/components`: a type-only import in `client/components/account/auth.ts`.

```10:10:client/components/account/auth.ts
import type { HttpTransportAuthProvider } from "@superfunctions/http";
```

That type is the return type of `createNucleumAuthFnTransportAuth`:

```80:84:client/components/account/auth.ts
export async function createNucleumAuthFnTransportAuth(
  input: AuthFnTransportAuthOptions = {}
): Promise<HttpTransportAuthProvider> {
  return (await authClient()).createTransportAuth(input);
}
```

There are no other imports or runtime usages of the package in `client/components`. The `package.json` entry is the only other mention.
